  m_text: 'A triangular prism is a prism made up of two triangular bases and three
    rectangular faces. The two triangular faces are congruent to each other and are
    called the base of the prism. The three rectangular faces are called the lateral
    faces.


    <b>Formula: <i>V = (1/2)bhl</i></b>'
