  m_text: "A cuboid is a 3D box-shaped geometric figure with six flat, rectangular
    faces and all corners meeting at 90\xB0 right angles. Everyday examples include
    bricks, shoeboxes, and cereal boxes. A cube is a special type of cuboid where
    all six faces are squares.\n\n<b>Formula: <i>V = lwh </i></b> "
