  m_text: 'Every three-dimensional object occupies some space. This space is measured
    in terms of its <color="orange"><b>volume</b></color>. Volume is defined as the
    space occupied within the boundaries of an object in three-dimensional space.
    It is also known as the capacity of the object.


    Different solids have different
    ways of solving their volume. Check out the volumes of each solids below.


'
